# MATH 4200 Exam 2 concept map (cyclic groups, permutations, cosets, isomorphisms).
title "MATH 4200 Exam 2"
root core

node core "Groups"
| set G + operation
| associative, identity e, inverses
| abelian: ab = ba
| order |G|, order |g|

node num "Integers\nand ℤ/nℤ"
node sub "Subgroups"
node cyc "Cyclic\ngroups"
node perm "Permutation\ngroups"
node cos "Cosets and\nLagrange"
node iso "Isomorphisms\nand products"

node divalg "Division Algorithm"
| a = bq + r, 0 ≤ r < b.
| Rests on Well-Ordering; induction.

node zn "ℤ/nℤ and (ℤ/nℤ)ˣ"
| [a] is a unit ⟺ gcd(a, n) = 1.
| |(ℤ/nℤ)ˣ| = φ(n).
| Repeated squaring for aᵏ mod n.

node bezout "gcd and Bézout"
| gcd(a, b) = ar + bs.
| gcd = 1 ⟺ ar + bs = 1.
| Euclidean algorithm computes r, s.

node phi "Euler φ"
| φ(n) = #{k ≤ n : gcd(k, n) = 1}.
| φ(pᵏ) = pᵏ − pᵏ⁻¹.
| φ(mn) = φ(m)φ(n) if gcd(m, n) = 1.

node primes "Primes"
| Euclid's Lemma: p | ab ⇒ p | a or p | b.
| Fundamental Thm of Arithmetic.
| Infinitely many primes.

node tests "Subgroup tests"
| Two-step: closed under products, inverses.
| One-step: gh⁻¹ ∈ H.
| Finite H: closure suffices.

node basic "Basic group facts"
| e and inverses unique.
| (ab)⁻¹ = b⁻¹a⁻¹. Cancellation.

node normal "Normal subgroups"
| H ⊴ G: ghg⁻¹ ∈ H for all g.
| ⟺ gH = Hg for all g.
| Abelian ⇒ every subgroup normal.
| V ⊴ S₄; S₃ ≤ S₄ not normal.

node gen "Generated subgroup ⟨a⟩"
| Smallest subgroup containing a.
| |a| = |⟨a⟩|.

node inter "Intersections and center"
| H ∩ K is a subgroup.
| gcd(|H|, |K|) = 1 ⇒ H ∩ K = {e}.
| Center Z(G) = {z : zg = gz ∀g}.

node elord "Order of an element"
| aᵏ = e ⟺ |a| divides k.
| |aᵏ| = n / gcd(k, n).
| |a| = ∞ ⇒ all powers distinct.

node abel "Cyclic ⇒ abelian"
| Converse false: ℤ/2ℤ × ℤ/2ℤ.
| ℚ, ℝ, ℤ × ℤ not cyclic.
| Subgroups of ℤ: nℤ.

node roots "Complex roots"
| z = re^{iθ}; De Moivre: zⁿ = rⁿe^{inθ}.
| zⁿ = Re^{iθ}: R^{1/n}e^{i(θ+2πk)/n}.
| nth roots of unity = ⟨e^{2πi/n}⟩.
| Primitive: e^{2πik/n}, gcd(k, n) = 1.

node gens "Generators"
| aᵏ generates ⟺ gcd(k, n) = 1.
| φ(n) generators; in ℤ/nℤ: [k].
| Cyclic (ℤ/mℤ)ˣ: φ(φ(m)) generators.

node ftcg "Fundamental Thm of Cyclic Groups"
| Every subgroup cyclic.
| Exactly one subgroup per d | n: ⟨a^{n/d}⟩.
| φ(d) elements of order d; Σ φ(d) = n.

node sn "Symmetric group Sₙ"
| |Sₙ| = n!. Disjoint cycle decomposition.
| Disjoint cycles commute.
| Order = lcm of cycle lengths.

node dih "Dihedral group D₂ₙ"
| Order 2n: rⁿ = s² = e, srs = r⁻¹.
| Center: {e} (n odd), {e, r^{n/2}} (n even).
| S₃ ≅ D₆; cube motions ≅ S₄.

node parity "Parity"
| Every σ = product of transpositions.
| Even/odd well-defined.
| k-cycle even ⟺ k odd.
| sgn(στ) = sgn(σ)sgn(τ).

node count "Counting in Sₙ"
| #k-cycles = n! / ((n − k)! · k).
| #cyclic subgroups of order p
| = #(order-p elements) / (p − 1).
| Conjugation preserves cycle type.

node an "Alternating group Aₙ"
| |Aₙ| = n!/2.
| Generated by 3-cycles.
| A₄: orders 1, 2, 3, 4, 12 only.

node cosets "Cosets"
| gH = {gh : h ∈ H}.
| Cosets partition G; |gH| = |H|.
| #left cosets = #right cosets.

node crit "Coset criteria"
| g₁H = g₂H ⟺ g₁⁻¹g₂ ∈ H
| ⟺ g₂ ∈ g₁H ⟺ Hg₁⁻¹ = Hg₂⁻¹.
| gH = H ⟺ g ∈ H.

node lagr "Lagrange's Theorem"
| H ≤ G finite ⇒ |H| divides |G|.
| [G : H] = |G| / |H|.
| [G : K] = [G : H][H : K].

node corr "Corollaries"
| |g| divides |G|; g^{|G|} = e.
| |G| = p ⇒ cyclic, any g ≠ e generates.
| No proper nontrivial subgroups
| ⇒ cyclic of prime order.

node euler "Euler and Fermat"
| gcd(a, n) = 1 ⇒ a^{φ(n)} ≡ 1 (mod n).
| p ∤ a ⇒ a^{p−1} ≡ 1 (mod p).
| Proof: Lagrange on (ℤ/nℤ)ˣ.

node conv "Converse fails"
| d | |G| does not force
| a subgroup of order d:
| A₄ has none of order 6.

node isodef "Isomorphism"
| Bijection, φ(ab) = φ(a)φ(b).
| φ(e) = e, φ(a⁻¹) = φ(a)⁻¹, |φ(a)| = |a|.
| ≅ is an equivalence relation.

node prod "Direct products"
| |(g, h)| = lcm(|g|, |h|).
| ℤ/mℤ × ℤ/nℤ ≅ ℤ/mnℤ ⟺ gcd(m, n) = 1.
| Internal: G = HK, H ∩ K = {e},
| hk = kh ⇒ G ≅ H × K.

node invar "Invariants (prove ≇)"
| Order, abelian, cyclic,
| # elements of each order, center.
| D₈ ≇ Q₈, D₁₂ ≇ A₄,
| ℤ/4ℤ ≇ ℤ/2ℤ × ℤ/2ℤ.

node classif "Classification"
| Cyclic ≅ ℤ or ℤ/nℤ.
| |G| = p ⇒ G ≅ ℤ/pℤ.
| Order 4: ℤ/4ℤ or ℤ/2ℤ × ℤ/2ℤ.
| Order 6: ℤ/6ℤ or S₃.

node units "Unit groups"
| (ℤ/mnℤ)ˣ ≅ (ℤ/mℤ)ˣ × (ℤ/nℤ)ˣ, gcd 1.
| Cyclic ⟺ m = 1, 2, 4, pᵏ, 2pᵏ.
| (ℤ/24ℤ)ˣ ≅ (ℤ/2ℤ)³.

node cayley "Cayley's Theorem"
| Every group ≅ a group of
| permutations, via g ↦ (x ↦ gx).

core -> num sub cyc perm cos iso
num -> divalg zn
divalg -> bezout
zn -> phi
bezout -> primes
sub -> tests basic normal
tests -> gen inter
cyc -> elord abel roots
elord -> gens ftcg
perm -> sn dih
sn -> parity count
parity -> an
cos -> cosets
cosets -> crit lagr
lagr -> corr euler conv
iso -> isodef prod
isodef -> invar classif cayley
prod -> units

gen ..> elord "cyclic case"
corr ..> classif "|G| = p"
conv ..> an "counterexample"
zn ..> units "structure"
